# Privacy and no retention

- Bind servers to `127.0.0.1`. Do not expose 0.0.0.0 in v1.
- No accounts, cookies that identify a person, analytics, newsletters, or email fields.
- Never persist prompts, answers, uploads, or filenames to disk, SQLite, or `localStorage`.
- Sessions live in process memory with a short TTL and die on restart.
- Logs may include method, path, status, and duration only — never request bodies or chunk text.
- v1 inference is Ollama on localhost. Do not add cloud LLM keys or hosted inference.

```python
# ❌ BAD
logger.info("question", extra={"q": body.question})
open("/tmp/upload.pdf", "wb").write(data)

# ✅ GOOD
logger.info("request", extra={"path": request.url.path, "status": 200})
parse_in_memory(data)
```
